-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/6a3b6d8a-d1d3-482c-b47e-f94a80b62f23
-- title:
--   Displays (12)–(13), p. 30 — E[𝓡*|𝓧_∅] = cE[𝓡] + dE[𝓩_∅|𝓧_∅] and Var(𝓡*|𝓧_∅) = Σ 𝓒_i² Var(𝓡) + d²Var(𝓩_∅|𝓧_∅)
-- statement:
--   Work in the delayed marked Galton–Watson model of the Setting with $c+d=1$, and assume the root has at least one inbound neighbour almost surely, $P(\mathcal N_\emptyset>0)=1$. Let $\mathcal R_i$ be the subtree opinions of display (7) and $\mathcal R=\mathcal R_1$. Then, almost surely,
--   $$E[\mathcal R^*\mid\boldsymbol{\mathcal X}_\emptyset]=E\Big[\sum_{i=1}^{\mathcal N_\emptyset}\mathcal C_i\mathcal R_i\,\Big|\,\boldsymbol{\mathcal X}_\emptyset\Big]+d\,E[\mathcal Z_\emptyset\mid\boldsymbol{\mathcal X}_\emptyset]=c\,E[\mathcal R]+d\,E[\mathcal Z_\emptyset\mid\boldsymbol{\mathcal X}_\emptyset],\tag{12}$$
--   $$\operatorname{Var}(\mathcal R^*\mid\boldsymbol{\mathcal X}_\emptyset)=\operatorname{Var}\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{\mathcal N_\emptyset}\mathcal C_i\mathcal R_i+d\mathcal Z_\emptyset\,\Big|\,\boldsymbol{\mathcal X}_\emptyset\Big)=\sum_{i=1}^{\mathcal N_\emptyset}\mathcal C_i^2\operatorname{Var}(\mathcal R)+d^2\operatorname{Var}(\mathcal Z_\emptyset\mid\boldsymbol{\mathcal X}_\emptyset).\tag{13}$$
--   Here $\mathcal Z_\emptyset=\mathcal Z_\emptyset^{(0)}$ is the root's signal at time 0, the one entering $\mathcal W_\emptyset^{(0)}$.
--
--   These identities separate the root's own randomness from that of its neighbours, and combined with (14) they give Proposition 5.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Conditioning is on the σ-algebra generated by $\boldsymbol{\mathcal X}_\emptyset$ (`markSigma X []`), and the conditional expectation and conditional variance are Mathlib's `condExp` and `condVar`, which are defined up to null sets; all four identities are equalities almost everywhere. The paper's $\mathcal R_i$ is `Rsub … [i-1] 1` (0-based) and $\mathcal R$ is `Rsub … [0] 1`. All variables are bounded, so no integrability hypothesis is needed. $P(\mathcal N_1>0)=1$ is not needed for these displays.
-- source:
--   Fraiman, Lin and Olvera-Cravioto, Opinion dynamics on directed complex networks, arXiv:2209.00969v2, p. 30, proof of Propositions 4 and 5, displays (12)–(13)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DirectedOpinion_NoMemory_Setting
open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace DirectedOpinion.NoMemory

/-- Displays (12) and (13), p. 30: conditional mean and variance of 𝓡* given 𝓧_∅, a.e.,
with 𝓡_i = `Rsub … [i] 1` (0-based) and 𝓡 = `Rsub … [0] 1`. -/
theorem eq_12_13 {Ω M : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] [MeasurableSpace M]
    (P : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure P] (mk : MarkFns M) (X : Label → Ω → M)
    (U : Label → ℕ → Ω → ℝ) (ζ : M → ℝ → ℝ) (c d : ℝ)
    (hgw : GWModel P mk X U ζ c d) (hcd : c + d = 1)
    (hN0 : ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, 0 < mk.N (X [] ω)) :
    let S : Ω → ℝ := fun ω =>
      ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (mk.N (X [] ω)), mk.C (X [] ω) i * Rsub mk X U ζ c d [i] 1 ω
    -- (12)
    (P[Rstar mk X U ζ c d | markSigma X []] =ᵐ[P] fun ω => P[S | markSigma X []] ω + d * P[Z X U ζ [] 0 | markSigma X []] ω) ∧
    ((fun ω => P[S | markSigma X []] ω + d * P[Z X U ζ [] 0 | markSigma X []] ω) =ᵐ[P]
      fun ω => c * ∫ ω', Rsub mk X U ζ c d [0] 1 ω' ∂P + d * P[Z X U ζ [] 0 | markSigma X []] ω) ∧
    -- (13)
    (Var[Rstar mk X U ζ c d; P | markSigma X []] =ᵐ[P] Var[fun ω => S ω + d * Z X U ζ [] 0 ω; P | markSigma X []]) ∧
    (Var[fun ω => S ω + d * Z X U ζ [] 0 ω; P | markSigma X []] =ᵐ[P]
      fun ω => (∑ i ∈ Finset.range (mk.N (X [] ω)), mk.C (X [] ω) i ^ 2) *
          variance (Rsub mk X U ζ c d [0] 1) P + d ^ 2 * Var[Z X U ζ [] 0; P | markSigma X []] ω) := by sorry

end DirectedOpinion.NoMemory
